BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Family Movies - The Day the Earth Blew Up a Looney Tunes Movie
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261128T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261128T130000
UID:6abfeab10f56a0002cd5248c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Every other Saturday Cliffcrest will be screening a free famil
 y friendly movie!\nThis months' movie:\nThe Day the Earth Blew Up a Looney
  Tunes Movie\nThat's not all folks! Porky Pig and Daffy Duck\, one of the 
 greatest comedic duos in history\, are making their hilarious return to th
 e big screen in this sci-fi comedy adventure. This is the first-ever fully
  animated Looney Tunes feature-length movie created for a cinema audience.
  Porky and Daffy are our unlikely heroes and Earth's only hope when facing
  the threat of alien invasion. In this buddy-comedy of epic proportions\, 
 they race to save the world\, delivering all the laugh-out-loud gags and v
 ibrant visuals that have made the Looney Tunes so iconic\, but on a scope 
 and scale yet to be experienced.
LOCATION:Cliffcrest
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abfeab10f56a0002cd5248c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Preschool
END:VEVENT
