BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Saturday Movie: The Girl Who Cried Pearls and Higglety Piggley
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270123T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270123T160000
UID:6a21a73a46d5f64f7dcdeff6@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Due to Hillcrest Library closure on July 27\, this event will
  be postponed until January 2027.\nIn Montreal\, at the dawn of the 20th c
 entury\, a poor boy falls in love with a girl whose sorrow turns into pear
 ls. He sells them to a ruthless pawnbroker\, who hungers for more. Tempted
  by greed\, the boy must choose between love and fortune. The choice could
  damn his soul.\nThe 2026 Oscar® Winner for Best Animated Short Film from
  the acclaimed team of Chris Lavis and Maciek Szczerbowski. This meticulo
 usly crafted film is a testament to the magic of stop-motion animation. Wi
 th handmade puppets\, mesmerizing narration by Colm Feore and a haunting s
 core by Patrick Watson\,\nThe Girl Who Cried Pearls\nis a timeless parable
  of desire\, deception and the price of innocence. (25 minutes)\nAlso scre
 ening from the same Oscar winning team with be\nHigglety Pigglety Pop! or 
 There Must Be More to Life\n. This live-action/animated adaptation of Maur
 ice Sendak's book features the voices of Meryl Streep and Forest Whitaker.
 \nThe story follows Jennie the terrier's suspenseful and unexpectedly mo
 ving journey to gain new experiences and realize her dream of becoming the
  star of the World Mother Goose Theatre. (23 minutes)\nFilms courtesy of t
 he National Film Board of Canada (NFB).\nDrop-in! No registration required
 .
LOCATION:Hillcrest\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a21a73a46d5f64f7dcdeff6
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Preschool
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
