DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261110T170000
UID:6ad7cd109d27a000455236e4@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Get creative with a fun\, hands-on art activity! Kids will use
  tape and paint to create colourful canvas masterpieces\, exploring patter
 ns\, shapes\, and their imagination. Once the tape is peeled away\, they
 ’ll reveal a unique work of art to take home and proudly display. No exp
 erience needed—just creativity and fun!\nAges 4-12\nRegistration Require
 d.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form 
 is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\
 , sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used fo
 r event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions abou
 t how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline s
 taff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto O
 N M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Danforth/Coxwell\, In the program room upstairs.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ad7cd109d27a000455236e4
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Preschool
