SUMMARY:Appleseed Yoga for Children and Families!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261128T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261128T120000
UID:6aba8b3fea50a10050a57ec5@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:​Join us for an interactive\, movement-based program where w
 e read stories and make them come alive with our bodies with\nMegan Snider
 \n! Megan Snider is an\nauthor\nand\nfounder\nof\nAppleseed Yoga for Kids\
 nwho\ndelivers inspiring stories and gets the whole family moving. Class b
 egins and ends with song and breathwork and is filled with pages of creati
 vity and activity.\nKids and families can sit quietly and listen\n\,\ndo p
 artial poses\nor make up their own\, following our lead.\nIt's ALL\nyoga!\
 nNo experience\, mats\, or materials required.\nThe program begins at\n11:
 00am\nuntil\nnoon\non\nSaturday November 28\, 2026.
LOCATION:Forest Hill\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aba8b3fea50a10050a57ec5
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Preschool
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Suddenly They Heard Footsteps: Storytelling with Dan Yashinsky
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261114T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261114T150000
UID:6aba91367c8c150075764bf3@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy the art of storytelling as Dan Yashinsky tells folktales
 \, riddles\, wisdom stories\, and yarns about his trouble-making Romanian-
 Jewish grandpa.  This\nall-ages program\nfeatures stories with suspense\, 
 surprises\, and hilarious suddenlies.  Bring your best riddles - there wil
 l be a contest!\nDan Yashinsky is a storyteller and writer based in Toront
 o.  His books include\nThe Golden Apples\n\,\nI Am Full – Stories for Ja
 cob\n\, and\nSuddenly They Heard Footsteps – Storytelling for the Twenty
 -first Century\n.  His upcoming book of donkey stories is called\nThe Stor
 yteller's Ass\n.  He has performed at festivals in Poland\, Estonia\, Indi
 a\, Brazil\, Hong Kong\, Belgium\, England\, Holland\, Czech Republic\, Wa
 les\, Ireland\, France\, Singapore\, Norway\, Sweden\, the US\, and throug
 hout Canada.\nPlease visit Forest Hill Toronto Public Library Branch Nove
 mber 14\, 2026 at 2:00pm - 3:00pm if you want to hear a story that keeps y
 ou on the edge of your seat!
LOCATION:Forest Hill\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aba91367c8c150075764bf3
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Preschool
END:VEVENT
